he right row fail to lift the fence because the digests differ, leaving a person fenced with no way out but a reload?\n2. The new memory key. It normalises trailing slashes in the service address. Can two addresses of one service differ another way, so that a page sends with no copy after a held session?\n3. An untraced refusal, in the note's limits. A newly enrolled third key with no session got forbidden on its signed read of the directory, and the build dropped that approach without tracing it. Is that a defect that this head must fix, or does it belong elsewhere?\n\nNo deployment is requested with this head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3a09e229161bc187eee56402b4360c384a41d6ed","branch":"builder/j1-design-20261031","conditions":"Independent exact-head review of d87ea2b1…6b6ca3a with explicit Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions, filed with gs review naming git:sha1…a41d6ed first and resting on all 38 artifacts.","head":"d87ea2b1010b6436400e5ff6db94f9b9d6b6ca3a","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"4817b532e7a1a118634cb7947b05f7d5d16f726c9d30ea22ff7eaf7db3634e80"}}